card.statement:
Consider the poset $\mathcal P=(1,1)$. The objects in $\mathcal P_{\chi}$-usp are those systems $(U;U_1,U_2)$ that satisfy

\begin{eqnarray*}
\chi_1 P_{U_1}+\chi_2 P_{U_2}=\chi_0 I.
\end{eqnarray*}

One can see that the projections $P_{U_1}$ and $P_{U_2}$ commute. Hence the indecomposable objects are at most one-dimensional. For the category $\mathcal P_{\chi}$-usp to be non-empty $\chi_0$ should be equal to $\chi_1+\chi_2$ (trace identity). Moreover, if this condition is satisfied then the indecomposables in $\mathcal
P_{\chi}-usp$ are in one-to-one correspondence with the indecomposables in $\mathcal P-sp$.
